---
// The manifesto: the long-form argument the homepage compresses. Same arc as
// docs/POSITIONING.md — the wound, the medium, the ritual, the loop.
import Logo from '../components/Logo.astro'
import WaitlistForm from '../components/WaitlistForm.astro'
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout
  title="why cedarpad exists — ideas in, decisions out"
  description="AI made building easy and decisions scarce. Chat is the wrong shape for deciding. Why we're building a shared board for deciding."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav aria-label="Main">
      <Logo />
      <div class="navlinks">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <a href="#waitlist">Access</a>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <article>
      <p class="label">Why cedarpad exists</p>
      <h1>Ideas in. Decisions out.</h1>

      <h2>The bottleneck moved</h2>
      <p>
        For seventy years, building software was the expensive part. Every tool we work in —
        tickets, specs, roadmaps — exists to protect scarce builder time. Then building stopped
        being scarce. One engineer with an AI agent ships in an afternoon what used to take a
        sprint.
      </p>
      <p>
        But watch a team of five, each vibe-coding with their own agent, and you see the new
        problem: they ship five afternoons of work in five directions. AI didn't just make
        building easy — it made misalignment cheap to produce at scale. The bottleneck moved
        upstream, to the oldest problem teams have: agreeing on what to build. Builders are
        everywhere now. Clear decisions are the scarce thing.
      </p>

      <h2>Chat is the wrong shape for deciding</h2>
      <p>
        The medium we got for working with AI is a chat thread: linear, single-player, gone by
        tomorrow. But almost everything worth deciding is structural — a system, a tradeoff
        space, three options and how they differ. Prose serializes structure; your head has to
        rebuild it. Whiteboards fixed structure but never finished anything: every session ends
        with someone photographing the board, and the real work restarting from zero somewhere
        else.
      </p>

      <h2>So we're building a board for deciding</h2>
      <p>
        Problems meet the team and its visual agents on one shared canvas. The agent answers in
        working things: research docs, diagrams, charts, custom apps, clickable prototypes.
        Everyone explores in parallel with their own agent; everything lands on one surface; the team converges by pointing at real things
        instead of arguing about adjectives.
      </p>

      <h2>Why this compounds</h2>
      <p>
        Every component your team builds becomes vocabulary — reusable words in how you and your
        agents communicate. A cedarpad workspace gets faster at aligning the longer it lives. A
        fresh chat window starts from zero every time.
      </p>

      <h2 id="waitlist">Come build it with us</h2>
      <p>
        Cedarpad is invite-only while we build it, and we sit with every team we let in.
      </p>
      <WaitlistForm id="why" />
    </article>

    <footer>
      <div>cedarpad — the pad where teams get aligned.</div>
      <div><a href="/changelog">Changelog</a> · © 2026 Zabaca</div>
    </footer>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  nav {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    padding: 20px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .navlinks {
    display: flex;
    gap: 22px;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
  }
  .navlinks a {
    color: var(--muted);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .navlinks a:hover {
    color: var(--text);
  }
  article {
    max-width: 640px;
    padding: 64px 0 72px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.4vw, 2.6rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.12;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 14px 0 8px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin: 44px 0 10px;
  }
  p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }
  footer {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding: 32px 0 48px;
    color: var(--faint);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 14px;
  }
  footer a {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  footer a:hover {
    color: var(--text);
  }
</style>
